  "name": "atx-v1/foreign-did-method-altered-after-signing",
  "description": "The foreign-did-method-valid.json credential with its agentDid changed after signing, from did:web:platform.example:agents:billing-agent to did:web:platform.example:agents:other-agent; every other member, both signatures included, is unchanged. agentDid is the second of the eleven fields the legacy canonical form signs (§1.3a.1), so the canonical bytes the verifier computes from this credential are not the bytes either signature covers, and the Ed25519 signature does not verify (§1.3 step 4). A verifier MUST REJECT with a signature-validation reason. The signature binds the credential to the subject identifier its issuer signed, under any DID method: a holder cannot move the credential to another identifier the same platform issues.",
  "requirement": "§1.3 step 4: the legacy canonical form signs agentDid as written (§1.3a.1), so a did:web agentDid changed after signing is a signature failure",
